< **The lifecycle markers**, all value-free, create-only, in the batch folder, in this order and no other: `BATCH_COMPLETE` (the driver) -> `SCORING_STARTED` (the scorer, before its first outcome read; it holds the score attempt id and the digest of the exact roster it will score) -> one score line per planned pair (create-only, in the Mode H score ledger) -> `SCORE_COMPLETE` (the scorer, after the last pair's line; it holds the ledger's digest) -> `MODE_H_SEALED` (the scorer, after the report; it holds the score attempt id, the ledger digest and the report's digest). The dispatch gate refuses any `REAL_HOLDOUT` publication once any of these exists; the updater refuses until `MODE_H_SEALED` exists (4.1). **Crash recovery is resumption of the same attempt, never a second one:** if the scorer stops after `SCORING_STARTED`, rerunning it finds that marker, re-verifies the same roster digest, skips every pair that already has a score line (it never re-reads an outcome for a pair already scored), scores the remaining pairs, then writes `SCORE_COMPLETE` and the seal; if it stops after `SCORE_COMPLETE`, rerunning it reads no outcome at all: if the attempt's report does not exist it writes the report from the accepted lines, and if it already exists it verifies the report's digest against the accepted lines and writes nothing new; then it writes the seal. The report carries the attempt id and no wall-clock field, so the resumed and the uninterrupted paths give the same report bytes. A second routine attempt is refused only when `SCORE_COMPLETE` exists; before that, the same attempt resumes. The ratified corrective exception (a separately identified scoring run beside the first, to correct a scorer fault or add a measure) is allowed after the seal, under its own identity, and never touches the first ledger.
