< - **A6 (single source; OWNER-DECIDED 3 November 2026, C03; the identity made exact, EX_127 C03):** production uses **one origin: scheme `https`, host exactly `www.lotterywest.wa.gov.au`**, and the one results-search page the updater already names (`gov_url`, lines 533-537, builds that host; today nothing checks the final host after redirects). The updater fetches through a browser driver (`BrowserFetcher`, line 540; `self.driver.get(url)`, line 567), and a browser follows redirects itself and exposes no status code, so v0.2 adds the check a browser allows: after the page loads and before any parse, lock or write, it refuses unless the browser's final URL (`driver.current_url`) has scheme `https` and host exactly `www.lotterywest.wa.gov.au` (a redirect to any other host is therefore refused after the browser followed it, with the final host named in the message), and it has **no fallback of any kind**: not `oz.lotterywest.com`, not The Lott, not an API, a mirror, a cache or an aggregator; a refusal means no row, no grab promoted, and the owner reads the message. **The owner has decided that Lotterywest's published results are official and trusted as they stand, so no second-source check of a new draw is required in production** (TSC-1 retires the two-site checker). What the updater's checks still prove, unchanged: that the fetched page agrees with every draw already held (overlap), that the new draws are consecutive and correctly dated, that the content parses to the closed grammar, and (by the chain check) that the master and its ledger agree; what they do not prove: that a newly appended draw matches any second source, nor which hosts the page's own sub-resources (scripts, images) were loaded from, which a browser decides and the updater does not inspect. This decision supersedes, for production, R2-C03's "independent evidence" and the proposal's candidate-then-promotion step; register v0.24 records it (Appendix K). The owner's private, by-hand check of The Lott stays his own and is never automated.
